WEBVTT

roster-1
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.579
Administrators manage staff
accounts and roles in one place.

roster-2
00:00:11.579 --> 00:00:14.583
The roster filters by role,
facility, and status,

roster-3
00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:17.649
and every change is audited
with the reason given.

least-privilege-1
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.986
Each user holds one role, and most
roles are scoped to a facility.

least-privilege-2
00:00:26.986 --> 00:00:29.459
Least privilege is enforced on the server:

least-privilege-3
00:00:29.459 --> 00:00:32.050
a facility admin can't
grant the admin role,

least-privilege-4
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.464
and an auditor sees the roster read only.

role-change-1
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.748
Changing a role takes a required reason.

role-change-2
00:00:44.748 --> 00:00:46.468
The change applies at once,

role-change-3
00:00:46.468 --> 00:00:50.035
and the history records who
changed what, when, and why.

credentials-1
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.840
The credential inventory lists every
service-to-service credential:

credentials-2
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.475
what it protects, who consumes it, who
rotates it, and the rotation target.

credentials-3
00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:08.515
It shows names and metadata only.

credentials-4
00:01:08.515 --> 00:01:11.110
No secret value is ever read or displayed.

rotation-1
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.463
Rotation age comes from value-free
metadata written at deploy time.

rotation-2
00:01:18.463 --> 00:01:23.436
This local stack has no deploy, so ages
show as unknown instead of being guessed.

phi-view-1
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.046
Every access to protected
health information is audited.

phi-view-2
00:01:32.046 --> 00:01:36.470
Opening the alert inbox records a view
for each synthetic patient on the screen.

phi-search-1
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.303
In the PHI access log, an admin filters
by date, user, action, resource,

phi-search-2
00:01:49.303 --> 00:01:51.144
or outcome, newest first.

phi-search-3
00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:54.458
The views from a moment
ago are already here.

paging-1
00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.437
Results come 50 at a time,
with an older-page cursor,

paging-2
00:02:03.437 --> 00:02:05.542
so even a large log stays quick.

paging-3
00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:08.502
Exports are capped, and
they're recorded too.

meta-audit-1
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.926
Viewing the log is itself logged.

meta-audit-2
00:02:17.926 --> 00:02:20.728
The audit row notes that
a user filter was used,

meta-audit-3
00:02:20.728 --> 00:02:23.005
never the email address that was typed.

closing-1
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:29.391
Least privilege, no secret values on
screen, and every PHI access audited:

closing-2
00:02:29.391 --> 00:02:31.684
governance an auditor can verify.

disclosure-1
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.710
A note on this recording: the
narration uses a synthetic voice,

disclosure-2
00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:41.186
and all data shown is synthetic demo
data, not a live customer deployment.
